## Configure OpenHPC in the Compute Image

`genimage` installed the OpenHPC core components above. The customization
chapters that follow -- node health checks, development tools, and optional
InfiniBand or GPU support -- install further packages into the compute image, so
first make their repositories available inside it. The freshly built image
carries the distro repositories disabled and neither the OpenHPC nor the EPEL
repository, so add them to the image:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Make the OpenHPC, EPEL, and base OS repos available in the image -->
```bash
# Copy the OpenHPC and EPEL repository definitions into the image
cp /etc/yum.repos.d/OpenHPC*.repo ${CHROOT}/etc/yum.repos.d
cp /etc/yum.repos.d/epel*.repo    ${CHROOT}/etc/yum.repos.d

# Enable the base OS repositories and CRB in the image (they ship disabled)
dnf --installroot="${CHROOT}" config-manager \
    --set-enabled baseos --set-enabled appstream --set-enabled crb
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

With the repositories in place, configure the OpenHPC services so the compute
nodes come up ready to join the cluster:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Configure OpenHPC services in the compute image -->
```bash
# Disable the firewall in the compute image
chroot ${CHROOT} systemctl disable firewalld

# Enable munge and slurmd to start on boot inside the compute image
chroot ${CHROOT} systemctl enable munge
chroot ${CHROOT} systemctl enable slurmd

# Register the Slurm server with the computes (configless mode)
echo SLURMD_OPTIONS="--conf-server ${sms_ip}" > ${CHROOT}/etc/sysconfig/slurmd
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
